BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Femmemoir: A zine-making workshop
DTSTART:20261017T130000
DTEND:20261017T130000
UID:1416c765e322ef46e224e12d6e660f24@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Led by the curators of the On Our Own Terms exhibition\, this 
 workshop offers the chance to explore zine-making as a medium for memoir a
 nd queer history. Zine-making experienced a renaissance in the 90s – the
  last analogue decade – and was strongly linked to DIY feminist and quee
 r activism\, including the queercore and riot grrrl movements. Come and le
 arn more about the history of queer zines and create your own “femmemoir
 ” – a mini personal and cultural archive. All materials will be provid
 ed. ‍
LOCATION:The ArQuives\, 34 Isabella Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/femmemoir-a-zine-making-workshop
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Autumn MEGA Book Swap
DTSTART:20261017T130000
DTEND:20261017T130000
UID:5e2ef5338087d6d79edc93ced46f50eb@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Mega Book Swap is a place for everyone to get books for fr
 ee or cheap. The Mega Book Swap is a place to get books for free or cheap.
  You swap your books for tickets you can use to trade for books. Even thou
 gh Glad Day’s focus is 2SLGBTQ books\, this Book Swap is for everyone an
 d (almost) every kind of book! Every book &#x27\;costs&#x27\; one ticket. 
 NEW! We are ALSO running a VINYL RECORD SWAP down the hall on the same day
  3pm-6pm! Info here: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/big-vinyl-record-swap-tic
 kets-2002921651577 Why RSVP or Prepay for Tickets RSVP for FREE in Eventbr
 ite and get entered into a draw to win 10 tickets! This helps us in our ev
 ent planning. Prepay for 3 tickets and skip any lines Want to prepay for t
 ickets and skip the line? Get 3 tickets for $10 in advance and we absorb t
 he Eventbrite &amp\; credit card fees for you :) Tickets will be held unde
 r your name. You ALSO get entered in a draw to win 10 more tickets! Timing
 : 12:30pm -Trading Books for Tickets starts 1pm - Ticket Mega Swap in the 
 Atrium starts 5pm - Last chance to trade in your books for tickets 6pm - E
 verything ends TWO WAYS TO SWAP! There are two ways to swap: Ticket Mega S
 wap (this is for 100s of books in the big Atrium space) Chaos Lounge Swap 
 (trade with actual people in the lounge) MEGA TICKET SWAP : How it works Y
 ou get tickets and you swap your ticket for a book from the big book zone 
 that will have over 400 books in it! The books will ‘cost’ just one ti
 cket. There will be tables spread out in the large Atrium and books will b
 e grouped roughly into areas like “Fiction”\, “Memoir”\, “Childr
 en’s” &quot\;French&quot\;\, &quot\;Health&quot\;. How to get tickets:
  You can BUY TICKETS You can buy 1 ticket for $5 or 3 tickets for $10 or Y
 ou can SWAP BOOKS FOR TICKETS 3 books gets you 1 ticket 5 books gets you 2
  tickets 10 books gets you 5 tickets Over 10 books get you 1 ticket for ev
 ery 2 books (see below for what books will not be accepted and which might
  get you extra tickets) Note: We expect there may be a 5-10 minute line to
  exchange your books for tickets\, so come early and avoid the line. Some 
 limits on what books can be swapped: You can swap almost any kind of book 
 that is in decent condition. It can be in rough shape but we won’t accep
 t anything with mold\, water damage or yucky to touch. Also\, the followin
 g books will not be accepted for tickets: Dictionaries or textbooks Refere
 nce books that are over 5 years old Outdated non-fiction like travel guide
 s\, health advice and self-help that are over 5 years old Magazines (unles
 s they are xxx magazines - we love those!) And these books will get you mo
 re tickets than normal (like 1 to 3 tickets per book) Queer books by BIPOC
  authors Children’s books with 2SLGBTQ content Trans books that are less
  than 10 years old Photography books Erotica Accessibility The entrance\, 
 space and washrooms are wheelchair accessible. ‍
LOCATION:Glad Day (32 Lisgar)\, 32 Lisgar
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/autumn-mega-book-swap
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
