BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exquisite Queer Corpses: Constructing Our Queer Selves with Mixed 
 Media Sculptures
DTSTART:20261018T120500
DTEND:20261018T120500
UID:10f2cc77671e42dfef354ead09b71a51@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the processes used for constructing the TQFF 10th 
 Year Anniversary poster\, artist Pardis Pahlavanlu leads a workshop where 
 participants can build their own queer subject sculptures using a mix of h
 and-building and found objects that Pardis will collect and share. After c
 hoosing their “body parts” and arranging them\, participants will adhe
 re their “body parts” using multiple traditional crafting methods (i.e
 . adhesive\, hand sewing\, etc.). Upon constructing their queer subject sc
 ulptures\, participants can place their characters on a green screen platf
 orm where they can take pictures of their creation. Through this workshop\
 , participants will capture the essence of intersectional queer embodiment
  without relying on the representation of queer subjects as a compilation 
 of stock human forms based on social categories. ‍
LOCATION:Tranzac Club\, 292 Brunswick Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/exquisite-queer-corpses-constructing-our-q
 ueer-selves-with-mixed-media-sculptures
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
