BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baila Sáfica Film Screening and Social Dancing
DTSTART:20261022T190000
DTEND:20261022T190000
UID:50d8529497c907d06a58a286a6bb8143@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:We are excited to welcome y&#x27\;all to our very first film s
 creening of &quot\;La Salsa Vive&quot\; Baila Sáfica presents &quot\;La S
 alsa Vive&quot\;: Telling the story of two cities bound by the rhythm of s
 alsa\, New York City and Cali\, Colombia\, La Salsa Vive is a vibrant cine
 matic exploration of the evolution of the style and a collective passion t
 hat has inspired generations. Featuring insights from salsa legends like s
 ingers Rubén Blades and Henry Fiol\, percussionists Samuel Formell\, John
 ny &quot\;Dandy&quot\; Rodríguez and orchestra conductor Willie Rosario\,
  and highlighting the dedicated dancers\, music collectors\, and enthusias
 tic youth who are united through music and dance\, La Salsa Vive is a puls
 ating journey through a vivid cultural history. Duration: 101 MIN. After t
 he documentary screening\, we will have a small social dancing to honour t
 he roots and feel the vibe of salsa! 🌈 Please read before getting your 
 ticket: Baila Safica is a sapphic salsa &amp\; bachata social created to o
 ffer a safe\, affirming space for sapphics to connect through dance\, musi
 c\, and community. If you do not identify with the sapphic experience\, we
  kindly ask that you sit out our events. This space is intentionally creat
 ed to center sapphic joy\, safety\, and community. This is a free event fo
 r our sapphic community\, but the tickets are limited. We ask people to re
 gister through the Eventbrite link so we have an idea of capacity. Doors o
 pen at 6:30 PM. Film Screening at 7:00 PM. We&#x27\;ll have some snacks\, 
 water\, and pop. We ask everyone to be respectful of the space and each ot
 her. We are creating a safe community\, and it means everyone who comes to
  our events belongs here\, no matter how they present! There is no room fo
 r harassment\, bullying\, prejudice\, or any type of violence! Organizers 
 reserve the right to remove anyone who makes others uncomfortable during t
 he event. If you have any questions\, DM us on Instagram @bailasaficatoron
 to. Come dance\, connect\, and celebrate with us💜 ‍
LOCATION:Glad Day (32 Lisgar)\, 32 Lisgar
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/baila-safica-film-screening-and-social-dan
 cing
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Buff-HeHehe - A Buffy the Vampire Slayer-Themed Comedy Show!
DTSTART:20261022T200000
DTEND:20261022T200000
UID:d72baaa5b404d3616bd211590acace84@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:An evening of Buffy themed live stand up comedy! Buffy fans - 
 this comedy show is for you! Some of Toronto&#x27\;s top comics will take 
 the stage to deliver Buffy-themed stand up comedy. Expect roasts of signat
 ure Buffy moments\, deep cuts\, and mutual nerding out about one of our fa
 vourite shows of all time! Costumes are encouraged (but not mandatory). Th
 ink your best Slayer-fit\, your favourite iconic Willow look\, or your fav
 ourite vampire from the Buffy cannon! Featuring: Anasimone Lou Currie Pete
 r Laneaus Bee Bertrand Hosted by Anna Penner (@somequeerreads\, HeHeHeated
  Rivalry) and Anna Sebastien (@annasebastiencomedy\, Tea4Tea All Trans Com
 edy\, Just for Laughs Toronto) Join us for a free screening of the Buffy M
 ovie after the show! ----- The venue: The show takes place in the theatre 
 space in the downstairs area of Tallboys. Take a left when you walk in and
  head downstairs! The venue unfortunately has a few barriers to access. Th
 ere is a large step to enter the main bar area. The theatre space and wash
 rooms are located down a staircase\, with tight corners from the bottom la
 nding to the theatre. There is also a single step from the basement hallwa
 y into the venue room. Once inside\, there is no grade change. There is a 
 communal gender neutral washroom with urinals and toilets\, a singe stall 
 unmarked gender neutral washroom with a toilet\, and a woman&#x27\;s washr
 oom with toilets. Seating is self-assigned and the venue is intimate\, so 
 we recommend groups arrive early so they can grab seats together Community
 : At this show we only speak to our own identities\, we don&#x27\;t punch 
 down\, and isms\, phobias\, and aggressive crowd work will never be tolera
 ted. This show is queer-forward\, and trans and queer inclusive AF. All we
 lcome including respectful allies. This is all about community amongst fel
 low Buffy-heads! If you are flying solo\, are nervous\, or have any questi
 ons\, feel free to DM the hosts @annasebastiencomedy and @somequeerreads o
 n Instagram. This is all about community! We all want a sexy\, healthy tim
 e right before Gay Christmas aka Halloween. If you are feeling sick\, plea
 se stay home! Refund requests will be honoured up to 12 hours before the s
 how. You are totally welcome to wear a mask\, and we&#x27\;d be stoked if 
 you rapid tested before the show. ‍
LOCATION:Tallboys Craft Beer House\, 838 Bloor Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/buff-hehehe---a-buffy-the-vampire-slayer-t
 hemed-comedy-show
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
