BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:¡A CENAAAR! An immersive Día de los Muertos dinner experience by
  machaa
DTSTART:20261029T190000
DTEND:20261029T190000
UID:68bd51afff5844700838d50f8827fcaf@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Step into 1940s Mexico for one night only. 30 seats\, music\, 
 theatre and the soul of a celebration. Bring a photo of someone you miss. 
 One night. One table. One house where the past comes to dinner. There’s 
 a house in Toronto that opens its doors just once a year. When you knock\,
  the host opens the door because they’ve been expecting you. Inside\, bo
 leros fill the room. Candlelight flickers against marigolds. An altar wait
 s for you to make it your own and honour someone who has passed\, someone 
 who will dine with us tonight. A long table is set\, and your seat is wait
 ing. Stories find their way to your eyes and ears. Characters live the nig
 ht beside you. Music drifts through the room. And somewhere between dinner
 \, theatre and memory\, you become part of the story. Welcome to the bohem
 ian Mexico of the 1940s\, inspired by the Golden Age of Mexican cinema\, t
 he intellectuals\, surrealists and muralists of an era defined by art\, im
 agination and exploration. ¡A Cenaaar! lives somewhere between a film and
  a dream. A night to dance\, remember\, and celebrate the past and the pre
 sent. There is no stage. No audience. No fourth wall. Come hungry. Bring a
  photo of someone you miss. Tonight\, no one dines alone. (FOR MORE INFO S
 EE THE TICKET LINK PROVIDED)
LOCATION:Foy House\, 92 Isabella St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/a-cenaaar-an-immersive-dia-de-los-muertos-
 dinner-experience-by-machaa
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Día de los Muertos Party with Spurs Night &amp\; Baila Sáfica
DTSTART:20261029T193000
DTEND:20261029T193000
UID:2b2f06b3bdba3db03ddccfca52dc7a82@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Dancing and Costume Contest @ Lula Lounge Thurs Oct 29th Doors
  7:30 Dancing 8pm-late Salsa\, bachata\, and line dance lessons all night 
 long! We are bringing together different cultures\, dance styles\, music g
 enres\, and spooky celebrations to bring you the ultimate queer party to k
 ick off Halloween weekend! Come celebrate Día de los Muertos with Spurs N
 ight and Baila Saficá at Lula Lounge. We will be teaching beginner line d
 ance\, salsa\, and bachata lessons\, along with hours of open dance floor 
 to keep things sexy and sweaty. Come learn a new form of dance or dance yo
 ur favourite style—there will be room on the dance floor for all genres 
 throughout the night. Halloween costumes and calavera makeup* encouraged f
 or our costume contest! *Calavera makeup is traditional Mexican skull make
 up worn during Día de los Muertos celebrations. If you aren&#x27\;t Mexic
 an or Latinx\, we&#x27\;re trusting you to pick your costume and makeup in
  a way that respects the wonderful but culturally sensitive traditions of 
 others. BIPOC Ticket Tier and PWYC Door Tickets We have reserved a number 
 of $15 tickets for BIPOC audience members. No one will be clocked on the d
 oor\; we trust people to self-identify for these tickets. There will be a 
 small number of door tickets available on the night. These (plus any remai
 ning online tickets) will be sold on a pay-what-you-can basis. Suggested p
 rice $15-20 but no one turned away for lack of funds! Accessibility Inform
 ation The front entrance to Lula is fully accessible. There is one step do
 wn onto the dance floor and one or two steps to the elevated dining areas.
  The venue has a movable ramp that allows wheelchairs and mobility devices
  to access the dance floor and the elevated dining area on the east side. 
 There is a fully accessible universal washroom on the main floor off the l
 obby. The coat check\, basement washrooms and mezzanine areas are not acce
 ssible. Requests related to accessibility can be directed to info@lula.ca.
  This event will not have a dedicated\, enclosed low-sensory room. However
 \, there will be a &quot\;chill out&quot\; space available in the mezzanin
 e\, with ample seating and away from dancing and flashing lights. This is 
 a Queer Party Please note that this event is open to all identities and au
 diences\, but it is a queer event. Respect the space and queers to the fro
 nt! There will be a zero tolerance for discrimination in any form. Spurs a
 nd Baila staff (and Lula&#x27\;s security team) will be on site to ensure 
 safeguarding of our community\, please don&#x27\;t hestiate to ask us for 
 help on the night. ‍
LOCATION:Lula Lounge\, 1585 Dundas Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/dia-de-los-muertos-party-with-spurs-night-
 baila-safica
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
